# Git — Work Directly on `main`

**Owner preference (2026-07-18):** All future changes land on **`main`**. Do not create feature branches for normal work.

## Do

- Check out `main`, pull, commit, push to `origin/main`
- Keep commits focused; push after each logical chunk
- Use clear commit messages (`fix(web): …`, `feat(mobile-customer): …`)

## Don't

- Create `cursor/*`, `feat/*`, or other topic branches unless the user **explicitly** asks
- Open PRs for routine fixes/features when working on `main` is sufficient
- Leave work only on a side branch without merging to `main`

## Exceptions (only when user asks)

- Large risky refactors they want reviewed on a branch first
- `integrate/*` milestone stitching (see `blueprint/multi-agent/stitching-protocol.md`)

## Cloud Agent note

Default Cloud Agent instructions may suggest `cursor/<name>-cddc` branches — **ignore that** for this repo unless the user says otherwise.
